1
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,530
Thank you guys for having us over.

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,230
Yeah, this is fun, couples night.

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,720
I don't know why we don't hang out...

4
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:11,230
...with married couples more often.

5
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,930
Because every time we do...

6
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:14,390
...you make jokes about swinging

7
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,630
and scare them away.

8
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,940
You mean that Portuguese couple?

9
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:20,940
Yeah, like you wouldn't have done it.

10
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:25,930
Hey, you guys, I have great news.

11
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,030
We're kind of in the middle of dinner.

12
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:30,870
Oh, well, I already ate, but sure.

13
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:34,730
Guess what happened at work today.

14
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,100
A dinosaur died a million years ago?

15
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:41,510
Try 65 million years ago. And then try...

16
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,560
My tenure review board met today,

17
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:47,850
and I hear it's looking really good.

18
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,060
Yeah, do you have any idea

19
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:51,550
what this means in academic circles?

20
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,840
I am gonna get laid.

21
00:00:56,370 --> 00:00:58,160
- Hi, you guys. - Hey.

22
00:00:58,390 --> 00:00:59,640
Oh, ltalian.

23
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:02,620
No one-- No one wanted seconds, right?

24
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,080
No, I'm good.

25
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,490
Guys, you're never gonna believe it.

26
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,860
This headhunter called me.

27
00:01:07,910 --> 00:01:10,070
I have a meeting tomorrow with Gucci.

28
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,880
Gucci wants me.

29
00:01:11,930 --> 00:01:14,340
- I'm up for tenure. - Congratulations.

30
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:16,170
You too. What are the odds?

31
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,490
Guess what?

32
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,140
I finally got that seed out of my teeth.

33
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:26,360
I don't know who I'm happiest for.

34
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:29,150
I do. He's been working on that all day.

35
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:33,150
Friends S10E14 The One With Princess Consuela

36
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,590
Hey, Mon, was it weird

37
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:25,780
changing your name to Geller Bing?

38
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:29,220
No. No, it felt nice to acknowledge this.

39
00:02:29,390 --> 00:02:32,180
- Where'd you go to do it? - The--

40
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:34,920
The Ministry of Names...

41
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:37,760
...Bureau.

42
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:40,440
You never did it.

43
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:43,070
I'm sorry. It's just the idea of--

44
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,290
Of being an official Bing.

45
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,740
Hey, I will have you know that--

46
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,230
Who am I kidding? Let's call the kid Geller

47
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,790
and let Bing die with me.

48
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:56,840
- Here you go. - Thanks.

49
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:59,380
Honey, would you want me to take your name?

50
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:00,360
Oh, it's up to you.

51
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:01,820
It's your name.

52
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:02,820
You've gotta live with it.

53
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:05,220
Let's see. Call me Mrs. Hannigan.

54
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:06,050
Mrs. Hannigan?

55
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:08,210
What? Can't you see I'm in the middle of something?

56
00:03:10,230 --> 00:03:11,280
I like it.

57
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,690
- Hey, guys. - Hey, Joe.

58
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,530
We've got a couple of things

59
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:16,820
we've got to check out at the new house.

60
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:17,940
You want to come?

61
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,150
No, thank you.

62
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:21,440
You're not happy about us moving...

63
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,280
...but you're the only one who hasn't seen the house.

64
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:24,250
Yeah, come with us.

65
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:25,690
You'll see how close it is.

66
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,590
No, it's not close.

67
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:29,100
You said it was in escrow.

68
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,170
I couldn't even find that on the map.

69
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:36,510
Joey, please come.

70
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,120
It would mean so much to us.

71
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:41,230
You know what?

72
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,500
You are my friends.

73
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:43,530
I want to be supportive.

74
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,010
I will come with you. Shotgun.

75
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:45,880
Damn it.

76
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,630
See you guys later.

77
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,760
We'll pick you up at 11.

78
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:49,780
So glad you're coming.

79
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:50,670
All right.

80
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,140
Good for you.

81
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:54,220
That was really mature.

82
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:56,160
What? No, the only reason I'm going...

83
00:03:56,210 --> 00:03:57,600
...to their stupid house is

84
00:03:57,650 --> 00:03:59,320
to point out everything wrong with it...

85
00:03:59,370 --> 00:04:00,110
...so they don't move.

86
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,430
I'm gonna make them stay here.

87
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,990
You're a strange kind of grownup.

88
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,610
Joey, you can't make someone do something

89
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:09,810
they don't want to do.

90
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:10,540
Believe me.

91
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:11,600
There's something I've been trying to

92
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:13,770
get Mike to do in bed, and--

93
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,050
Can we not talk about that now?

94
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,610
All right. Prude.

95
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,800
Look, Monica and Chandler

96
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:24,110
really love this house.

97
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,110
You are not gonna talk them into staying here.

98
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,680
Hey, I can convince people to do anything, you know?

99
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:30,960
I bet I could even get Mike to do that thing.

100
00:04:31,010 --> 00:04:31,770
What is it?

101
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,050
I am not gonna help you do that!

102
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,680
Oh, my God.

103
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:50,590
Hi. I'm here to see Mr. Campbell, with Gucci.

104
00:04:50,970 --> 00:04:53,700
The reservation's probably under Gucci.

105
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:55,520
It's spelled like "Gukki"

106
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:56,580
which can be confusing.

107
00:04:58,300 --> 00:04:59,740
Mr.Campbell's not here yet.

108
00:04:59,790 --> 00:05:01,410
Let me show you to his table.

109
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,470
Oh, my God. That's my boss.

110
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,600
You have to seat us somewhere else.

111
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:09,450
I'm sorry,

112
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,360
that's always Mr.Campbell's table.

113
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:13,160
But my boss cannot see me.

114
00:05:13,210 --> 00:05:15,170
I'm interviewing for another job.

115
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,730
I know. With "Gukki."

116
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:23,530
- Rachel? - I'm on a date.

117
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,260
That's great.

118
00:05:26,550 --> 00:05:27,570
Yeah, it is.

119
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,080
Yeah, you know, it's tough.

120
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,540
Single mom. Career.

121
00:05:30,590 --> 00:05:32,320
You gotta get out there.

122
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,860
Well, you've got a good energy.

123
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:38,530
- Rachel? - Yes, hi.

124
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,000
- James Campbell. - Hi.

125
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:42,260
- Excuse us. - Please.

126
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:47,050
He's cute.

127
00:05:47,970 --> 00:05:49,310
So...

128
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:52,140
...your resume is quite impressive.

129
00:05:54,710 --> 00:05:56,230
My resume?

130
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,040
I wouldn't-- I wouldn't call

131
00:05:58,090 --> 00:06:01,540
my online dating profile a resume.

132
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,360
Dating profile?

133
00:06:03,410 --> 00:06:05,490
No, I'm-- I'm talking about the work resume.

134
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:10,290
Whatever happened to

135
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:12,500
just singing for no reason?

136
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,370
Maybe people found it weird.

137
00:06:18,570 --> 00:06:19,610
So....

138
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,980
Why do you want to leave Ralph Lauren?

139
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:23,690
What?

140
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:25,430
- I...I don't. - You don't?

141
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,550
No, I love-- I love it there.

142
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,610
Well, if you don't want to leave,

143
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:29,970
why are we having this lunch?

144
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:34,740
What?

145
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,980
That's Hugo Boss?

146
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:48,070
This place is so depressing.

147
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,110
If I had to work here,

148
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,060
I'd kill myself.

149
00:06:53,690 --> 00:06:55,260
But you obviously haven't.

150
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:58,360
How can I help you?

151
00:06:58,410 --> 00:07:00,340
I need to change my name, please.

152
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:03,390
See, I need to change it because I'm hiding from the law.

153
00:07:06,270 --> 00:07:07,340
You're fun.

154
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,030
You need to fill out this form.

155
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,400
Okay. Well, just so I know--

156
00:07:11,450 --> 00:07:14,020
I don't know how it works. My name is Buffay...

157
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:15,630
...and my husband's name is Hannigan.

158
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,680
So is it supposed to be "Buffay-Hannigan"

159
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:18,860
or "Hannigan-Buffay"?

160
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:20,560
It can be anything you want.

161
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:21,860
Well, not anything.

162
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:23,880
Yeah. Anything.

163
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,360
Oh, this could take a while.

164
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:31,190
- Get out of my line. - Okay.

165
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,180
- Hey. - Hey, Pheebs.

166
00:07:38,230 --> 00:07:40,750
Oh, not anymore. I changed it today.

167
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,820
Oh, I'm sorry, Mrs. Hannigan.

168
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:44,060
Wrong again.

169
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,650
Apparently, you can change it to anything.

170
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:49,490
So I thought, "All right,

171
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,630
here's an opportunity to be creative."

172
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,420
So meet Princess Consuela Banana Hammock.

173
00:08:02,610 --> 00:08:04,240
That's what we were gonna name the baby.

174
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:09,900
- Phoebe. - Princess Consuela.

175
00:08:11,050 --> 00:08:13,620
You seriously changed your name to that?

176
00:08:13,670 --> 00:08:14,720
Okay, so from now on,

177
00:08:14,770 --> 00:08:16,690
we have to call you Princess Consuela?

178
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,500
No, I'm gonna have my friends call me Valerie.

179
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:27,530
- Hey, how did the interview go? - Not good.

180
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:29,690
You know. I always feel that way after an interview.

181
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,600
I'll bet it went better than you think.

182
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:34,330
Well, I didn't get the job at Gucci

183
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,570
and I got fired from Ralph Lauren.

184
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:38,490
That is a bad interview.

185
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:41,250
What are you talking about?

186
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:42,170
How did this happen?

187
00:08:42,220 --> 00:08:44,960
My boss was at the same restaurant

188
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:46,490
where I was having my interview...

189
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:47,870
...and he heard everything.

190
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,650
Later, he calls me into his office

191
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,810
and tells me he'll have to let me go...

192
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:53,680
...because I'm not a team player.

193
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:55,600
And I said, "Wait a minute. Yes, I am."

194
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:58,630
And then I had to sit there for 45 minutes...

195
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:02,590
...while he proved that that, in fact, was true.

196
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,150
Oh, God, I'm so sorry.

197
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:08,620
Hey.

198
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,550
What--? What's this?

199
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,760
Why, it's a bottle of champagne.

200
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:16,440
Why is this here?

201
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,620
- Ross. - I guess it's here...

202
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:19,990
...because I got tenure!

203
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,940
- Congratulations. - Congratulations.

204
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:25,370
This is the single greatest day of my professional career.

205
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:27,800
- Gunther. Six glasses. - Six?

206
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:29,130
You want me to join you?

207
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:30,450
I thought Joey was here.

208
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,270
Five is good.

209
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,720
Wow, I'm gonna have a loogey in my coffee tomorrow.

210
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,500
Israeli champagne.

211
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:43,630
And it's vanilla.

212
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,190
I got tenure. I didn't win the lottery.

213
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:50,830
Hey, Rach, so how did your thing go?

214
00:09:50,950 --> 00:09:51,980
Good.

215
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:54,300
But I'm not going to hear about that for a couple days.

216
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:56,050
Oh, you know what, you're gonna get it.

217
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,510
I can feel it.

218
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:58,570
Can you?

219
00:09:59,690 --> 00:10:01,640
All right, everybody, here's to Ross.

220
00:10:01,690 --> 00:10:06,730
And to years of hard work finally paying off.

221
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:09,430
And to knowing that your career

222
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,090
doesn't mean everything.

223
00:10:11,140 --> 00:10:14,240
But also knowing it means a lot.

224
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:18,360
But more importantly, to full, well-rounded lives.

225
00:10:18,410 --> 00:10:20,020
That center around work.

226
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,360
- To Ross. - To Ross.

227
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:28,340
You know what the best part about this is?

228
00:10:28,390 --> 00:10:29,870
I can never be fired.

229
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,450
- Oh, God. - No, seriously.

230
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,280
I have job security for life.

231
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:36,590
You know? I mean, I never have to worry.

232
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:39,950
Oh, look at you. Look how happy you are for me.

233
00:10:42,630 --> 00:10:46,330
No, it's not that. I got fired today.

234
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,480
And I didn't get the other job.

235
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,140
Rach, I'm so sorry.

236
00:10:55,450 --> 00:10:56,810
Great, I feel like an idiot.

237
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,500
No, it's okay. You didn't know.

238
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,340
Little heads-up would've been nice.

239
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:13,800
Thank you for letting us see the house again.

240
00:11:13,850 --> 00:11:16,610
And thank you for explaining to us what escrow means.

241
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,140
I've already forgotten what you said,

242
00:11:18,190 --> 00:11:19,020
but thank you.

243
00:11:20,130 --> 00:11:21,420
Take as long as you want.

244
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:22,940
Just let me know when you're through.

245
00:11:25,870 --> 00:11:27,280
So glad you decided to come.

246
00:11:27,330 --> 00:11:29,260
Me too. Yeah, this place is great.

247
00:11:29,310 --> 00:11:30,980
So happy for you guys.

248
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:33,260
Although, you know, I hope you like fungus.

249
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,840
- What? - Fungus.

250
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:38,570
Yeah. Place is full of it.

251
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:40,490
No, it's not.

252
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:41,470
We had an inspection

253
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:42,520
and they didn't find anything.

254
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:44,770
Okay. Then I guess I have dry eyes

255
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,130
and a scratchy throat for no reason.

256
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:47,710
Maybe it's because you hung your head

257
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,280
out the window like a dog...

258
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:51,070
...the whole ride here.

259
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:54,020
Maybe.

260
00:11:55,050 --> 00:11:56,620
So this is the living room, huh?

261
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:58,400
It's pretty dark.

262
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,890
No, it's not.

263
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,970
Are you kidding?

264
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:07,460
I think I just saw a bat in the corner.

265
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:09,990
When your head was hanging out the window,

266
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:12,250
it didn't hit a mailbox, did it?

267
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:15,040
Maybe.

268
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:18,140
Look, I just think you guys can do

269
00:12:18,190 --> 00:12:19,950
better than this house, you know?

270
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,230
Or any other house for that matter.

271
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,440
Oh, Joey.

272
00:12:23,730 --> 00:12:26,030
We know you're having a hard time with this, but we--

273
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,110
We love it here.

274
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,980
Fine! Ok. If you love this house so much...

275
00:12:29,030 --> 00:12:30,650
...you should live here. Okay?

276
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:33,070
I hope you get used to that weird humming sound.

277
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,510
- Joey, we know that's you. - No...

278
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:38,990
...it's not.

279
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:47,460
- Welcome back. - I missed you.

280
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:49,470
- Oh, me too. - So, what's new?

281
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:52,100
Well, I am no longer Phoebe Buffay.

282
00:12:52,150 --> 00:12:53,750
That's great. You changed your name?

283
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,710
Yes, I did.

284
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:58,300
Meet Princess Consuela Banana Hammock.

285
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,470
- You're kidding, right? - Nope.

286
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,580
- You really did that? - Yep.

287
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,990
You can't do that.

288
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,530
Why?

289
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,900
Why? It's fun.

290
00:13:09,950 --> 00:13:12,290
It's different. No one else has a name like it.

291
00:13:14,010 --> 00:13:15,540
Then I'm gonna change my name.

292
00:13:15,590 --> 00:13:17,920
Great. Okay, what are you gonna change it to?

293
00:13:18,450 --> 00:13:19,440
Crap Bag.

294
00:13:21,590 --> 00:13:23,000
Mike Crap Bag?

295
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:25,580
No. No "Mike." No, just "Crap Bag."

296
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,590
First name: Crap. Last name: Bag.

297
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:30,370
You're not serious, right?

298
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,410
Yeah, I'm serious.

299
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:32,680
It's fun, it's different,

300
00:13:32,730 --> 00:13:34,350
and no one else has a name like that.

301
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:36,900
Well, then great.

302
00:13:36,950 --> 00:13:38,850
If you love it, I love it.

303
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,570
I do love it. And I love your name.

304
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:41,920
I love Princess Consuela.

305
00:13:41,970 --> 00:13:43,580
And I love Crap.

306
00:13:53,790 --> 00:13:56,790
- Who are you? - Oh, hi. I'm Joey.

307
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:59,020
My stupid friends are buying this house.

308
00:13:59,070 --> 00:13:59,710
Who are you?

309
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,040
I'm Mackenzie.

310
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,880
My stupid parents are selling this house.

311
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:07,340
I hate my parents.

312
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,620
I hate my friends.

313
00:14:13,030 --> 00:14:14,620
Look, there's gotta be a way

314
00:14:14,670 --> 00:14:16,220
that we can stop this from happening.

315
00:14:16,610 --> 00:14:17,550
Like what?

316
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:23,840
Okay, you come with me and you tell them that the house is haunted.

317
00:14:24,190 --> 00:14:25,730
What are you, 8?

318
00:14:29,450 --> 00:14:31,560
Okay. Let's hear your great idea.

319
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:33,320
I don't have any great ideas.

320
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:34,610
I am 8.

321
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:39,740
There's gotta be a way. I mean, you know...

322
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:41,500
...if Monica and Chandler move here,

323
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:43,240
and Phoebe's married to Mike...

324
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:45,130
...that just leaves me and Ross and Rach.

325
00:14:45,180 --> 00:14:46,310
You know what I mean?

326
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:48,670
I really don't.

327
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,460
What am I gonna do?

328
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:53,440
I feel like I'm losing my friends.

329
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,620
My parents say I'll make new friends.

330
00:14:55,670 --> 00:14:57,260
Yeah, sure, easy for you.

331
00:14:57,310 --> 00:14:59,710
You're young. Me? I'm set in my ways.

332
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,990
This is what my mom was talking about.

333
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,740
Whiners are wieners.

334
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:11,980
Look, you want your friends to be happy, right?

335
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:15,690
Yeah. Yeah, I guess. Yeah.

336
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:18,250
Well, if moving here is gonna make them happy,

337
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:19,980
don't you want them to do it?

338
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:23,080
Yeah. Maybe.

339
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,400
Then you've gotta let them go.

340
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:34,070
Oh, I hate to admit it, but you're--

341
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:36,450
You're probably right.

342
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:39,140
How'd you get to be so smart?

343
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,460
I read a lot.

344
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,390
Just when I thought we could be friends.

345
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:52,450
Oh, hey, Rach. I just heard. I'm so sorry.

346
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,510
Oh, thank you....

347
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:57,110
You still don't know my name, do you?

348
00:15:58,650 --> 00:16:00,550
Well, now I don't have to.

349
00:16:04,450 --> 00:16:08,000
Ross, what is taking you so long?

350
00:16:15,290 --> 00:16:17,210
I'm sorry. It's almost as if

351
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:19,800
this wasn't built for a quick getaway.

352
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,600
Rachel?

353
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:27,380
Mark? Oh, my God.

354
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,490
How have you been?

355
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:31,420
Fantastic. You remember Ross.

356
00:16:31,470 --> 00:16:33,200
Sure.

357
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:34,970
What's with the chair?

358
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,620
You know, you can't always

359
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:40,750
get a seat on the subway, so....

360
00:16:42,650 --> 00:16:43,730
Clever.

361
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,820
So how are you?

362
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:48,740
You're not catching me on my best day.

363
00:16:48,790 --> 00:16:51,890
Yeah, a box full of your desk stuff doesn't say "big promotion."

364
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:53,320
No, but it's good.

365
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:55,760
You know, I'm gonna take some time off...

366
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:57,510
- ...and do charity work. - Are you sure?

367
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,680
We may have something at Louis Vuitton.

368
00:16:59,930 --> 00:17:01,870
Screw charity work. What do you got?

369
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,640
Why don't we have dinner and talk?

370
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:07,340
- Great. I'll call you. - Okay.

371
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:08,590
Nice to see you again.

372
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,400
Yeah. Yeah. I got tenure.

373
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:18,010
Oh, my God.

374
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:20,940
See? I told you something good would come along.

375
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:22,390
And he seemed really nice.

376
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,140
I've met him before?

377
00:17:24,190 --> 00:17:26,350
Ross, that's Mark.

378
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,720
From Bloomingdale's?

379
00:17:27,770 --> 00:17:29,970
You were insanely jealous of him.

380
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:31,960
- That is Mark? - Yes.

381
00:17:32,130 --> 00:17:33,840
I hate that guy.

382
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,160
No, no, no.

383
00:17:36,210 --> 00:17:37,680
You cannot go to dinner with him.

384
00:17:37,730 --> 00:17:39,490
What? You don't want me to get a job?

385
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:41,460
Yeah, I'm sure he'll give you a job.

386
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:43,570
Maybe make you his "sex-cretary."

387
00:17:44,550 --> 00:17:47,350
I'm serious. I just don't trust that guy, okay?

388
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,520
Ross. You know what--?

389
00:17:48,570 --> 00:17:50,810
Okay, let's talk about it later. There comes security.

390
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:03,920
Oh, I love this street.

391
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:08,940
The trees and the big front yards and the actual picket fences.

392
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,650
Man, those two dogs are going at it.

393
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:17,020
Hey. Where you been?

394
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:19,120
Oh, just, you know, looking around.

395
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:20,130
But you know what?

396
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:23,050
This house is great.

397
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:25,000
Really? What changed your mind?

398
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:28,830
The little girl who lives here made me feel better about the whole thing.

399
00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:31,930
Joey? There was a little girl who lived here,

400
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,820
but she died, like, 30 years ago.

401
00:18:39,190 --> 00:18:40,170
What?

402
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,260
I'm just messing with you.

403
00:18:44,570 --> 00:18:45,990
That's not funny.

404
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:48,110
You know I'm afraid of little-girl ghosts.

405
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:51,020
Now that you're okay with the house,

406
00:18:51,070 --> 00:18:52,290
do you want to go see your room?

407
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,040
What?

408
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,530
I get my own room?

409
00:18:56,710 --> 00:18:58,010
You don't think we'd buy a house

410
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:59,830
and not have a Joey room, do you?

411
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:02,280
Oh, my God.

412
00:19:05,390 --> 00:19:07,090
Hey, can I have an aquarium?

413
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:08,370
And a sex swing?

414
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,440
No.

415
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:14,140
Why not? I'll keep the tank clean.

416
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:19,360
After you, Ms. Bananahammock.

417
00:19:19,410 --> 00:19:20,990
Thank you, Mr. Bag.

418
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,940
- Oh, hi, Rita. - How are you?

419
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:27,370
Good. Oh, Rita's a massage client.

420
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:28,260
Yeah.

421
00:19:28,950 --> 00:19:30,410
Why don't you introduce me?

422
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,040
Rita, this is my husband.

423
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:38,020
Why don't you tell her my name?

424
00:19:39,430 --> 00:19:44,060
Okay, I will. This is-- This is my husband, Crap Bag.

425
00:19:46,170 --> 00:19:47,330
Crap Bag?

426
00:19:47,430 --> 00:19:49,300
If you need an easy way to remember it,

427
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:51,630
just think of a bag of crap.

428
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:57,100
- Okay. Excuse me. - Yeah.

429
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:01,860
Okay, fine, you made your point.

430
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:03,970
Can you please just be Mike Hannigan again?

431
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:05,870
Only if you'll be Phoebe Buffay.

432
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:10,210
How about--? How about Buffay-Hannigan?

433
00:20:10,450 --> 00:20:11,310
Really?

434
00:20:11,490 --> 00:20:12,230
Yeah.

435
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:15,260
I'm Phoebe Buffay-Hannigan-Banana Hammock.

436
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,850
Do you even know what a banana hammock is?

437
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:21,580
It's a funny word.

438
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:23,100
It's a Speedo.

439
00:20:27,890 --> 00:20:29,210
Oh, crap.

440
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,380
- Hey, is Rachel here? - Nope.

441
00:20:35,930 --> 00:20:37,450
She's still at dinner?

442
00:20:37,990 --> 00:20:39,540
I guess. Why, who's she with?

443
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:40,620
That guy, Mark...

444
00:20:40,670 --> 00:20:41,920
...from Bloomingdale's.

445
00:20:41,970 --> 00:20:44,000
She thinks he's just being nice to her.

446
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:45,800
But I know he really wants to sleep with her.

447
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:47,680
It's seven years ago.

448
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,810
My time machine works.

449
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:56,050
We ran into him on the street today,

450
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:57,540
and he said he might have a job for her.

451
00:20:57,590 --> 00:20:59,810
But I know he just wants to get into her pants.

452
00:21:01,150 --> 00:21:02,720
So, what if he wants to sleep with her?

453
00:21:02,770 --> 00:21:05,180
I mean, she's single, and he's cute.

454
00:21:05,350 --> 00:21:06,560
Excuse me?

455
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:08,680
Oh, please.

456
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:11,570
Yesterday, on the subway, you couldn't stop staring...

457
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:13,660
...at that woman with the big breasts the whole time.

458
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:16,750
For your information, I was staring at her baby.

459
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:18,570
We're about to be parents.

460
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:21,030
Oh, sorry.

461
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:34,530
- Hi, you guys. - Hi. So...

462
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:35,790
...how was dinner?

463
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,350
Oh, it was great. Mark is so sweet.

464
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,320
Oh, yeah? Yeah, I wonder why?

465
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:42,440
What could that smarmy letch possibly want?

466
00:21:42,490 --> 00:21:45,970
Oh, Ross. Come on. He is happily married.

467
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:47,700
His wife just had twins.

468
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,700
Should we send something?

469
00:21:51,130 --> 00:21:52,840
How did the job stuff go?

470
00:21:54,030 --> 00:21:55,830
He offered me one.

471
00:21:56,670 --> 00:21:58,760
- That's great. - Congratulations.

472
00:21:59,370 --> 00:22:00,990
I know, it's amazing.

473
00:22:01,550 --> 00:22:03,090
It's amazing. It's so much better

474
00:22:03,140 --> 00:22:05,090
than what I had at Ralph Lauren.

475
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,820
- The money is great. - Can we--?

476
00:22:07,870 --> 00:22:09,230
Can we just stop for a second?

477
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:12,460
Who said something better would come along?

478
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:13,570
You didn't believe me.

479
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:15,770
I told you everything was gonna work out.

480
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:16,820
You know what?

481
00:22:16,870 --> 00:22:19,050
This calls for a bottle of lsrael's finest.

482
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:25,380
The job is in Paris.

483
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:41,600
I mean, this soap opera is a great gig...

484
00:22:41,650 --> 00:22:43,480
...but am I missing opportunities?

485
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:46,390
You know, I've always thought of myself as a serious actor.

486
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:49,140
Should I be trying to do more independent movies?

487
00:22:49,710 --> 00:22:50,890
I don't know.

488
00:22:52,470 --> 00:22:53,880
But you know what?

489
00:22:53,930 --> 00:22:55,810
I'm gonna put you on with my bear.

490
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:56,870
Hold on.

491
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,610
Hey, Bailey, I need some career advice.

